msgid "Policy · M7Technical · T7PolicyDay 1M1M2M3Day 2M4M5M6M7TechnicalDay 1T1T2T3T4T5Day 2T6T7 Day 2 · 11:30–16:15 · Technical module 7 · serves M7Team build, showcase and the journey togetherDraftCan each team change one app in the journey and then run the whole journey live, from a birth abroad to a clinic back home to the family travelling again? SessionsTeam build11:30–12:30 · 60 minTeam build, part 1Each team takes one app in the journey. Everything is pre-configured, so there is no Android Studio. You run the app, read how its configuration works, and change it. Test with the vaccination cards.LeadsRoy Munge, Elly Nandi, Fikri, Simon Njoroge · SupportsOne per teamTeam build13:30–14:25 · 55 minTeam build, part 2Finish the change, test it with the cards, and get ready to show it.LeadsRoy Munge, Elly Nandi, Fikri, Simon Njoroge · SupportsOne per teamShowcase14:25–15:00 · 35 minTeam presentationsEach team shows what it built, about seven minutes each. Volunteers present.LeadsFred Hersch (chair)ProposedTeam build15:30–16:15 · 45 minPutting the journey togetherVolunteers run the whole journey on the demo system, each using their own piece. This is the rehearsal for the finale.LeadsRoy Munge, Simon Njoroge · SupportsA volunteer from each teamProposed By the end you canRun your app and find where its configuration livesMake one change and see it workHave a working piece you can show in under seven minutes Where it meets the journeyJ2bRegistered at home, and referredWhat the system doesCHW app team: the registration form, the household, the referral.Technical questionWhich one configuration change would make the CHW app fit your country's household register?J3aThe clinic confirms the cards are genuineWhat the system doesClinic app team: the verifier and its trust store.Technical questionHow would your clinic app load your country's trust list, and how often would it refresh it?J4.0aOne phone holds the whole family’s recordsWhat the system doesFamily app team: one phone, one profile and one link per member.Technical questionHow should the family app separate each member's records on a shared phone?J4.1A Taifafeki doctor sees the full historyWhat the system doesViewer app team: open the link, enter the passcode, read the records.Technical questionWhat must the viewer show the clinician about where the records came from? Technical questions for the roomJ2bWhich one configuration change would make the CHW app fit your country's household register?J3aHow would your clinic app load your country's trust list, and how often would it refresh it?J4.0aHow should the family app separate each member's records on a shared phone?J4.1What must the viewer show the clinician about where the records came from? The four teamsCHW appThe health worker's phoneScan a vaccination card, add the child to the household, and refer them to a clinic.J2a J2bClinic appThe nurse's tabletReceive the referral, verify the card against the trust list, and plan the next visit.J3a J3bFamily appThe parent's phoneHold the family's records and share a child's record as a health link.J4.0a J4.0bViewer appThe clinic abroadOpen a shared health link and read the records behind it.J4.1 Terms at those stepsClient RegistryCivil registration and vital statisticsPoint-of-Service ApplicationsFacility, workforce and product registriesConsentInteroperabilityTrust listGlobal Digital Health Certification NetworkTrust anchorPublic key infrastructureDigital signatureIssuer · holder · verifierVerifiable credentialDigital walletPersonal health recordLifelong Health RecordInternational Patient SummaryHealth information exchange M7 First move and the investment requiredModule × journey mapAll modules"
